1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Why didn't anyone tell me my
son was failing the school year?

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:08,000
I did tell her. Three times.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Both are telling the truth.

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,000
But the warnings got lost along the way.

5
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,000
A note in a backpack.

6
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,000
A message half-delivered.

7
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:20,000
A school summons no one signed.

8
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Each one was a warning sign.

9
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:25,000
And none arrived in time.

10
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Why not just a chat?

11
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Because in Guayaquil, a teacher's number
can end up in the hands of a gang.

12
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Teachers get threatened and
extorted for giving a fair grade.

13
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:43,000
That's why many no longer
give out their number.

14
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:47,000
Meanwhile, a kid drifting away from class

15
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:51,000
gets closer to the
streets, and to the gangs.

16
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:56,000
No one should have to choose
between warning parents in time

17
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:58,000
and keeping their own family safe.

18
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:00,000
That's why we built Cresco.

19
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:04,000
One: the teacher writes
it down the same day.

20
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:11,000
And the family gets the alert
instantly, without the child's name.

21
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:17,000
And there's a record of who saw
it: the paper trail builds itself.

22
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:21,000
Two: families take part,
and no one is anonymous.

23
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:27,000
They reply by name; the
teacher answers in writing.

24
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:31,000
And three: all of it, without
exposing personal information.

25
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:35,000
Cresco is free, with ads for families.

26
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:38,000
Thanks to RevenueCat, each
gets their own extra:

27
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:41,000
teachers with PRO reach more classes;

28
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:45,000
families with Premium better
understand how to help their child.

29
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:47,000
I did tell her.

30
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:49,000
And I got there in time.

31
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:54,000
We're starting in Guayaquil.
Next: every classroom in Ecuador.

32
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:57,000
Cresco: so no warning
sign arrives too late.
